 "payload": {
  "attribution": "Salazar, Saxena, Baker, Kwek, Kyaw, arXiv:2608.14798v1; asserted by the authors in the paper text",
  "comparison_baseline": "Haar-random states and $\nu$-compressible states",
  "components": [
   {
    "component_id": "comp:thm",
    "role": "CONCLUSION",
    "source_span_refs": [
     {
      "content_hash": "sha256:73fe4d3bf997a05acabe354567984a7e007d4568e39aa2bbc0ced47140c9253e",
      "record_id": "span:opus5-2608.14798v1/sps-thm",
      "record_type": "agtxiv.v3.source-span/0.0.0",
      "revision": 1
     }
    ],
    "text": "Closed-form ensemble SPF for SPS at $|S|=2^n$."
   },
   {
    "component_id": "comp:nullity",
    "role": "CONCLUSION",
    "source_span_refs": [
     {
      "content_hash": "sha256:38b1b34d7c8c0569a53f46c711a837d9566a023ff4f96f5c62535b3488d4408a",
      "record_id": "span:opus5-2608.14798v1/sps-nullity",
      "record_type": "agtxiv.v3.source-span/0.0.0",
      "revision": 1
     }
    ],
    "text": "Nullity does not separate SPS from Haar states; both have $\\nu=\\mathcal{O}(n)$."
   },
   {
    "component_id": "comp:crypto",
    "role": "LIMITATION",
    "source_span_refs": [
     {
      "content_hash": "sha256:38b1b34d7c8c0569a53f46c711a837d9566a023ff4f96f5c62535b3488d4408a",
      "record_id": "span:opus5-2608.14798v1/sps-nullity",
      "record_type": "agtxiv.v3.source-span/0.0.0",
      "revision": 1
     }
    ],
    "text": "Efficient $\\nu$-extraction must not translate into efficiently distinguishing SPS from Haar, else the pseudomagic definition would be contradicted."
   },
   {
    "component_id": "comp:tunable",
    "role": "CONCLUSION",
    "source_span_refs": [
     {
      "content_hash": "sha256:73fe4d3bf997a05acabe354567984a7e007d4568e39aa2bbc0ced47140c9253e",
      "record_id": "span:opus5-2608.14798v1/sps-thm",
      "record_type": "agtxiv.v3.source-span/0.0.0",
      "revision": 1
     }
    ],
    "text": "Applying Cliffords tunes the entanglement of SPS while keeping magic content unchanged."
   },
   {
    "component_id": "comp:randomf",
    "role": "ASSUMPTION",
    "source_span_refs": [
     {
      "content_hash": "sha256:62aaf6dafe3043b7b461e25b2507e70e64ac88d70cf9d43d265939d08a6a8e6e",
      "record_id": "span:opus5-2608.14798v1/sps-random-f",
      "record_type": "agtxiv.v3.source-span/0.0.0",
      "revision": 1
     }
    ],
    "text": "The supplemental derivation averages over a UNIFORMLY RANDOM Boolean function $f$ (the cumulant lemma says so explicitly), not over a pseudorandom one."
   },
   {
    "component_id": "comp:density",
    "role": "EVIDENCE",
    "source_span_refs": [
     {
      "content_hash": "sha256:d01b2baed2e65d02799b780b5effd7ee89a052352d8950d593296b03b9fb4c08",
      "record_id": "span:opus5-2608.14798v1/sps-numerics",
      "record_type": "agtxiv.v3.source-span/0.0.0",
      "revision": 1
     }
    ],
    "text": "A corollary gives the exact average SPS Pauli-spectrum density, a sum of delta peaks that does not smooth out under ensemble averaging, unlike the Haar case; it is checked numerically against exact Pauli expectations for $n\\in\\{2,4,6,8\\}$, exhaustively over Boolean functions for $n=2,4$ and over 4096 and 2048 random functions for $n=6,8$."
   }
  ],
  "conditions": [
   {
    "condition_id": "cond:size",
    "origin": "SOURCE_EXPLICIT",
    "source_span_refs": [
     {
      "content_hash": "sha256:c67b7fd77ac0492da16489f10643e132e3fecac68a905eea3473c38473c0696e",
      "record_id": "span:opus5-2608.14798v1/sps-def",
      "record_type": "agtxiv.v3.source-span/0.0.0",
      "revision": 1
     }
    ],
    "statement": "the theorem is restricted to $|S|=2^n$, the single-subset case, where only the average over pseudorandom $f$ remains"
   },
   {
    "condition_id": "cond:avg",
    "origin": "SOURCE_EXPLICIT",
    "source_span_refs": [
     {
      "content_hash": "sha256:c67b7fd77ac0492da16489f10643e132e3fecac68a905eea3473c38473c0696e",
      "record_id": "span:opus5-2608.14798v1/sps-def",
      "record_type": "agtxiv.v3.source-span/0.0.0",
      "revision": 1
     }
    ],
    "statement": "the result is an ensemble average over the SPS family"
   }
  ],
  "modality": "ASSERTED",
  "source_span_refs": [
   {
    "content_hash": "sha256:c67b7fd77ac0492da16489f10643e132e3fecac68a905eea3473c38473c0696e",
    "record_id": "span:opus5-2608.14798v1/sps-def",
    "record_type": "agtxiv.v3.source-span/0.0.0",
    "revision": 1
   },
   {
